X:3
T:Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star
O:France
C:tune traditional (France, "Ah! vous dirai-je, maman"); words: Jane Taylor (1806)
R:lullaby
S:traditional, as commonly sung in classrooms
M:4/4
L:1/4
K:C
%%style ballad
!mf!(C C G G | A A G2 | F F E E | D D C2) | (G G F F | E E D2 | G G F F | E E D2) | (C C G G | A A G2 | F F E E | D D C2) |]
w: Twin-kle, twin-kle, lit-tle star, how I won-der what you are. Up a-bove the world so high, like a dia-mond in the sky. Twin-kle, twin-kle, lit-tle star, how I won-der what you are.

