X:6
T:Amazing Grace
S:traditional, as commonly sung in classrooms
C:Words: John Newton (1779); tune: New Britain (USA, 1829)
O:USA
R:hymn
M:3/4
L:1/4
K:G
%%style ballad
!mp!(D | G2 (B/2G/2) | B2 A | G2 E | D2) (D | !<(!G2 (B/2G/2) | B2 A | !<)!d3- | d2) !mf!((B/2d/2) |
w: A-ma-zing_ grace, how sweet the sound that saved a_ wretch like me, _ I_
d2 (B/2G/2) | B2 A | G2 E | D2) (D | !>(!G2 (B/2G/2) | B2 A | !>)!G3- | G2) |]
w: once was_ lost but now am found, was blind but_ now I see. _

